=== layout: one-panel

# *Binomial Distribution*

@body

- In statistics, the binomial distribution give the probability of the number of successes in a sequence of [*n*]{underline=true} independent [*yes/no experiments*]{underline=true}, each of which yields success with probability [*p*]{underline=true}.

@notes

Source: lect07b-prob_of_progeny.odp, slide 16.

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Binomial coefficient*

@body

- is often read aloud as "[n choose k]{underline=true}", because there are    ways to choose k elements, disregarding their order, from a set of n elements.

@notes

Source: lect07b-prob_of_progeny.odp, slide 17.
